      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for comment. According to [Java practice](go/java-practices/null#annotations)\nFor @Nullable: You don\u0027t have to use it, but if you do, use it consistently throughout your class, target, or, ideally, package ... otherwise presence of any @Nullable annotations may lead users to falsely assume that any unannotated element is definitely non-null.\n\nI agree it is a good practice to annotate so, but it is a big change and out of scope of this patch.",
